{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Who brings forth chariot and horse, army [and mighty].</b> Weighty and mighty on dry land, and they are the Chaldeans who go out to fight the Persians:" "<b>They are extinguished.</b> From a binyan whose object is not named, and its form is like כבו, and likewise ידעך נרו באשון חשך (Proverbs 20:20):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:46.780991449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}